  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves the development of a database system for a university to manage information related to students, professors, and courses. This system is designed to support academic administration and research activities by capturing data about academic capabilities, course evaluations, and registration details.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe main objective is to provide university administrators, faculty members, and students with a comprehensive database that enables efficient management of courses, student progress, and faculty data. It aims to facilitate data-driven decision-making and optimize educational outcomes through structured data handling.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- University Administrators: Responsible for overseeing academic and administrative processes.\n- Professors: Utilize the system to manage their research assistants and evaluate teaching effectiveness.\n- Students: Use the system for course registration and accessing academic performance records.\n- IT Staff: Maintain and support the system infrastructure.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Student Management: \n   - Maintain records of student intelligence and academic ranking.\n   - Enable student registration for courses.\n   - Track student grades and satisfaction levels with courses.\n\n2. Professor Management: \n   - Record professor popularity and teaching ability metrics.\n   - Allow professors to manage research assistants, including capability assessment and salary details.\n\n3. Course Management: \n   - Store and manage course information, including difficulty and student ratings.\n   - Ensure association of students with courses and maintain their registration records.\n\n4. Registration Handling: \n   - Enable sorting of courses registered by each student.\n   - Track and store grades and satisfaction metrics for students in each course.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- The system should ensure data integrity and security, especially when handling personal and academic information.\n- It should provide high availability and support scalability for a large number of concurrent users.\n- Interfaces should be user-friendly to ensure ease of access and manipulation of data by both technical and non-technical users.\n- The system must comply with relevant legal and ethical standards for data privacy and protection.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0136\nCREATE TABLE `students` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `student_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `intelligence_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `academic_rank` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `professors` (\n  `professor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `professor_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `teaching_ability_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`professor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `courses` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `difficulty_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `student_rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `professor_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`),\n  KEY `courses_ibfk_1` (`professor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `courses_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`professor_id`) REFERENCES `professors` (`professor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `registrations` (\n  `registration_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `grade` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `satisfaction_score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_order` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`registration_id`),\n  KEY `registrations_ibfk_1` (`student_id`),\n  KEY `registrations_ibfk_2` (`course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `registrations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `students` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `registrations_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `research_assistants` (\n  `assistant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `assistant_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `professor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `capability_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `salary` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`assistant_id`),\n  KEY `research_assistants_ibfk_1` (`professor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `research_assistants_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`professor_id`) REFERENCES `professors` (`professor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
